  "query_preview": "..\nIssued 130 PM CDT Sat May 9 2026\n\nMonday night through Saturday:\n\nModels continue to support a fairly strong shortwave trough and\nassociated wave of low pressure tracking from Canada to central\nWI on Tue. A well organized swly low level jet of 45-50 kt and \nwarm, moist advection pattern will bring sufficient moisture and\nlift for widespread rain and perhaps scattered elevated convection.\nThere will be just low chances for sfc based convection with the\ncold frontal passage late Tue afternoon and evening. \n\nHigh pressure will then follow for Wed nt-Thu AM followed by a\njet stream pattern change to quasi-zonal for late next week. \nThis will bring a return of warm and humid conditions and \nincreasing rain chances. \n\nGehring",
